{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/216858-so-any-chance-of-new-material-for-promethean","id":216858,"title":"So any chance of new material for Promethean?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-02T13:34:43-07:00","id":216858,"title":"So any chance of new material for Promethean?","content":"I realize there is that combo book coming out (or is out already), but anything specific for promethean? <br /> <br /> Promethean is by far the most underrated of the settings (just look at the number of posts), but by far my personal favorite.<br /> <br /> I just hope that Bill Bridges, Conrad Hubbard, Justin Achilli, Chuck Wendig, etc, etc. could become demiurges and breathe new life into PTC. Now that would be some alchemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T14:21:03-07:00","id":216920,"title":"","content":"More <i>Promethean</i> is definitely something I'd like us to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T16:16:27-07:00","id":217027,"title":"","content":"Well you have a small, but dedicated fan base. I own almost every PTC product (all 5 books), the pdf adventure (to the flames or something), and the GM's screen. I think I am just missing the character sheet pads. Any pdf / hardcover products you put out, I will buy (I am more of a hardcover book kinda guy though).<br /> <br /> I'd LOVE to see a revised / re-imagined PTC, maybe adding more definition to the milestone / humanity system while simplifying the torment / wasteland / disquiet systems. The idea of having a soulful quest for humanity is still a theme I'd like in the game though. As a ST, I Ioved mapping out the milestones for each character while leaving them somewhat open to interpretation. <br /> <br /> While it ties better with the GMC, I'd like to see qashmallim removed - just my personal two cents. There is so much else going on that I saw the qashmallim as a distraction and I have never seen deux ex machina contrivances work well in a tabletop setting. Plus, I am not the most religious person - so having these enigmatic angels giving cryptic messages or quests didn't really seem salient.<br /> <br /> There are several different awesome ways it could go. Anyways that is just my vote.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T17:47:35-07:00","id":217078,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">There\u2019s a rumor (still unconfirmed AFAIK) that Matt McFarland(?) may be working on something <b>Promethean</b>-related \u2014 possibly a Chronicle book with which to relaunch the line. He wrote the Promethean chapter of <b>Mortal Remains</b>, which could be thought of as a \u201cbeta test\u201d for new rules concerning Disquiet and Wasteland. The upcoming <b>Dark Eras</b> book will also have an enrty for Prometheans: from what I\u2019ve heard, it will cover the Dust Bowl Depression-era (e.g., <i>Grapes of Wrath</i>).</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The soulful quest for humanity is so central a theme to the game that it wouldn\u2019t be <b>Promethean</b> without it. However, I feel that the game could benefit from diversifying the ways that that theme can be expressed. I\u2019ve seen it described by some as an allegory for childhood and growing up; but to the extent that it is, it\u2019s almost always framed in terms of being an orphan growing up on the streets. I\u2019d like to see demiurges be a bigger element of the game, to facilitate messy parent/child dynamics and rebellion-against-authority story options as the Created seeks to establish an identity for himself apart from a creator who doesn\u2019t understand him. Not that you\u2019d be forced to do this, mind you; but as things stand now, the troubled relationship between Frankenstein and his monster or between Pygmalion and Galatea, etc., are regulated to the status of ancient parables that might never have even happened, save only for the existence of the Lineages; I want the new core book to support such stories as something you can <i>play out</i>, and without having to recast the Frankenstein/Pygmalion figure as an older Promethean.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">I <i>don\u2019t</i> want to see <i>qashmallim</i> purged from the book; as is, they\u2019re enough on the fringes of the game that if you don\u2019t like them, it\u2019s easy enough to not use them. But if you <i>do</i> have uses for them, it\u2019s nice to have them available.</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T18:20:19-07:00","id":217092,"title":"","content":"Grapes of Wrath? Well hopefully the chronicle doesn't end with a pandoran sucking azoth out of a galateid... Okay BAD IMAGE. So the Dark Era for PTC is going to be the depression 30's era? Sweet! <br /> <br /> Yeah I shied away from Mortal Remains since it is more of a Hunter line book... I do own 2 hunter products (core book plus Slasher), but I haven't really ever played in it. But maybe I'll check it out just for the Prommie stuff.<br /> <br /> Qashmallim are definitely arguable and a matter of taste. I just didn't care much for them and everyone I spoke to about them didn't really like the concept either. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T21:07:46-07:00","id":217149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/216858-so-any-chance-of-new-material-for-promethean?p=216920#post216920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More <i>Promethean</i> is definitely something I'd like us to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I heartily endorse this product or event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T21:46:05-07:00","id":217173,"title":"","content":"10/10 would buy. Twice. Just like my current PTC core. Would probably buy 3 so players can read it while I still own a copy.<br /> <br /> Please: more Promethean","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T22:17:57-07:00","id":217180,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see a Chronicle book for Promethean; none of my friends will give it a fair chance and something as wonderful and cohesive as Blood &amp; Smoke might go a fair way towards changing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","val